  "articleBody": "Getting easy access drawers installed correctly makes a huge difference in your kitchen or bathroom, but it's easy to make a few slip-ups. Here are some common mistakes and how to avoid them: \n1. **Choosing the wrong slide length:** This is crucial! If your slides are too short, your drawer won't extend fully, defeating the 'easy access' purpose. Measure your cabinet depth and drawer length carefully. \n2. **Misplacing the slides:** The slides need to be mounted at the correct height and depth to allow for full extension. Even a small error here can impact how far the drawer opens. \n3. **Failing to check for side-to-side parallelism:** If your slides aren't perfectly parallel, the drawer will bind, stick, and just generally be a pain to open and close. Use a level and take your time. \n4. **Overlooking interference from screws or cabinet parts:** Make sure all screws are flush and that there's nothing inside the cabinet or near the drawer that could obstruct its movement. \n5. **Not considering the load rating:** If you plan to store heavy items, you need slides designed to handle that weight. Otherwise, your 'easy access' drawer will quickly sag and fail. If you're unsure about any of these steps, especially with tight spaces or custom needs, HH Remodeling LLC can help ensure a perfect, frustration-free installation.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
